The pointwise meet of two approximable maps, whose elementwise action is intersection of filters.

<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`interMap`).** The pointwise intersection of two approximable maps relates neighbourhoods precisely when both components do.

*Proof.* Master, intersection, and monotonicity hold componentwise. ∎

**Theorem (`mem_toElementMap_interMap`).** The elementwise action of the pointwise intersection is the intersection of the elementwise actions.

*Proof.* One direction splits a common witness; the converse intersects the two witnessing neighbourhoods and uses monotonicity. ∎
